  "about": [
    "External libraries compiled into the pinned FFmpeg builds (runtimes.json), for THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES/ffmpeg.txt and scripts/fetch_gpl_sources.py (spec §15, R-08).",
    "Versions are copied from the builders' own records: win-x64 from README.txt inside the Gyan.dev archive (section \"external libraries' versions\"), macOS from versions.txt next to each martin-riedl.de download.",
    "Each library has 'fetch' when an exact source archive could be located (a release tarball, a tag, or the commit named in the builder's version string), or 'not_covered' saying why not.",
    "Sources are fetched for every copyleft library (GPL, LGPL, MPL). Permissive libraries (BSD, MIT, ISC, Zlib, Apache) are listed with their upstream but not fetched: their licences ask for notices, not source.",
    "A fetch with 'git' clones the repository and archives the named revision; 'url' downloads the archive as is."
